# Same bytes on every OS. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would
# check text out as CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere; the checker's regexes, offsets and
# test-set sizes must not depend on where the repo was cloned. CRLF input is tested on
# purpose, with fixtures built in the test, never by accident of checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
